node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
# `coverage/` above targets test-coverage output; don't let it swallow the app source
# directory of the same name (Floating-SE Territory page lives here).
!apps/admin/src/pages/coverage/
.turbo/
apps/backend/dist/
packages/shared/dist/
# TS incremental build cache — churns on every build, must not be tracked (#114 §8)
*.tsbuildinfo
apps/mobile/.expo/
package-lock.json


.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log

# Docs are now VERSIONED for disaster-recovery (#115): the PRD, business workflow, audits,
# architecture docs, ADRs, UI reference imagery, progress/handoff reports, and SYSTEM-STATE
# live only on one disk otherwise. Policy: track the whole docs/ tree. Secrets stay out via
# the `.env` rules above (they match at any depth); no credentials live under docs/.
.scratch/*
!.scratch/fsm-platform-v1/
# .claude/ is machine-local by default, EXCEPT the agent machinery the documented process
# depends on: a fresh clone must be able to run the context-budget / rolling-handoff loop
# (docs/agents/workflow.md). Same #115 reasoning as docs/. settings.local.json (permissions),
# state/ (per-session scratch) and worktrees/ stay out.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/context-budget.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/__pycache__/
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/handoff/
!.claude/skills/autohandoff/
!.claude/skills/implement/
!.claude/skills/tdd/
# Repo-root artifact dirs only — anchored with a leading `/` so they no longer shadow source
# paths that happen to be named `data`/`backups` (e.g. apps/admin/src/components/data/, #114).
/data/
/backups/

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
apps/backend/src/generated/

# #218c — the live-batch stand-down export (`--export-standdown` on the departure dry-run) regenerates
# on every read-only rehearsal and holds real production ticket/device/vehicle rows. Deliberately never
# staged; ignored explicitly so a future `git add -A` cannot sweep it in. The rest of
# `audit/autoplant-reconciliation/` (reports, plans, the Excel benchmark) is tracked on purpose.
audit/autoplant-reconciliation/standdown-live-batches.csv

# The installer-quality analysis. Deliberately never staged, for the same reason as the stand-down
# export above: it is real data about named parties, and here the naming IS the harm. The headline
# finding — `PRATIK PAWAR`, 79 installs / 97.5% never-online — is NOT a person doing bad work; it is
# a single 2h27m bulk-provisioning session across four states, a third-party vendor feed that was
# never physically connected. SUMMARY.md says so explicitly, but the directory name, the filenames
# and a `git log -S` six months from now do not, and a named account sitting in history next to a
# 97.5% failure rate reads as an accusation to everyone who never opens the file. The CSVs also
# carry real plant, transporter and vehicle rows. The analysis is kept on disk and shared directly,
# out of band. Do not re-add it because `git status` looks untidy.
audit/installer-quality-2026-08/
